# The ending embers_of_the_fallen (data/endings/embers_of_the_fallen.json): the narration the ending screen plays before its slides. The Vagrant tells it
# afterwards: second person, present tense, one or two sentences a line, no game words. First draft by Claude; Gemini edits it.

~ start
Narrator: The goat skull takes what was given, every last bit of it, and the moon pulls the Crooked Queen up into itself like a tide going out.
Narrator: The Crooked Tree burns, and in its light you count who's standing beside you, and you count again, because the number's wrong.
Narrator: You carry them home in your own way, in a story you'll tell as long as you've got breath to tell it.
Narrator: At the old platform the whistle comes out of the mist, and the train pulls in with more seats than you need.
the_vagrant: I saved their places. Seemed only right. Climb on, now.
